Now that you have Stormbringer you can forget about Cleaver, unless
you're keeping pets and don't want to kill them by accident.  I would
keep going with SB until you find a silver sabre.  Then become skilled
in the sabre and two-weaponing.  SB and a silver sabre at +7 is almost
as good as it gets.  At that point the shield will be irrelevant.

I would do what you're already doing with the daggers.  Tossing a few
+7 daggers and zapping wands should be sufficient for ranged attack,
then when they get close enough to two-weapon with SB and a sabre they
won't know what hit them.

The only question is whether you're satisfied with SB until the end of
the game.  If not, just get Basic in the broadsword, use it for a
while, and wish for Frost Brand or something else later.



